    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create a Python script that generates a time-limited signed download URL for a stored object, I need to choose a concrete external provider. Amazon S3 is a widely used service for storing objects and provides a straightforward way to generate presigned URLs. I will use the Boto3 library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, to interact with S3. The script will include the necessary imports and code to generate a presigned URL. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789850023234,
          "start": 1789850020757
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bb5feb95001eBN6uu1wOqAgm8",
